<title>FRANCE: Carbone Lorraine stock rebounds.</title>
<headline>Carbone Lorraine stock rebounds.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Carbone Lorraine rose on Monday, recovering part of their fall on Friday, after the metals group expressed confidence in its performance this year at an analysts' meeting, brokers said.</p>
<p>The shares were up 2.12 percent at 1,250 francs in a flat market. The stock fell 4.4 percent on Friday after aluminium giant Pechiney said it would sell its 37.7 percent stake.</p>
<p>Last Thursday, Carbone Lorraine reported a profit of 136 million francs, up from 83 million in 1995, on sales of 3.09 billion. Analysts were told sales were expected to rise in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
